From: chickendrop89 <chickendrop89@github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] apex: fix SM5602 fuel gauge probe reliability

Return -EPROBE_DEFER when GPIO is invalid so the probe is retried.

Signed-off-by: apex project
diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/nopmi/sm5602_fg.c b/drivers/power/supply/nopmi/sm5602_fg.c
index b1c0468b7..bd27c46f0 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/nopmi/sm5602_fg.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/nopmi/sm5602_fg.c
@@ -4702,8 +4702,9 @@ static int fg_common_parse_dt(struct sm_fg_chip *sm)
 	pr_info("gpio_int=%d\n", sm->gpio_int);
 
 	if (!gpio_is_valid(sm->gpio_int)) {
-		pr_info("gpio_int is not valid\n");
+		pr_info("gpio_int is not valid, deferring probe\n");
 		sm->gpio_int = -EINVAL;
+		return -EPROBE_DEFER;
 	}
 #endif
     /* EN TEMP EX/IN */
